#N canvas 20 20 4000 2700 12;
#X text 20 20 m_organelle -- the Organelle's OWN front panel \, mapped like any other device. mother.pd publishes aux and the four knobs on reserved names \; this turns them into named controls on param and disp \, and knows nothing about what any of them does. Same layer \, same rules and the same silence about meaning as m_nano. Everything about this module is on ref/device/organelle.md., f 58;
#X text 20 170 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r aux;
#X obj 260 300 r knob1;
#X obj 500 300 r knob2;
#X obj 740 300 r knob3;
#X obj 980 300 r knob4;
#X obj 420 420 select 1 0;
#X obj 260 350 change -1;
#X obj 500 350 change -1;
#X obj 740 350 change -1;
#X obj 980 350 change -1;
#X msg 420 480 modal shift;
#X msg 260 410 og-knob-1 \$1;
#X msg 500 410 og-knob-2 \$1;
#X msg 740 410 og-knob-3 \$1;
#X msg 980 410 og-knob-4 \$1;
#X obj 1330 520 t f f;
#X obj 20 580 s disp;
#X obj 220 580 s param;
#X text 20 660 THE og- PREFIX IS NOT DECORATION. m_nano already publishes knob-1 to knob-9 \, and a single hyphen is not a distinction anyone can be trusted to read inside a route box. The Organelle's own knobs are og-knob-1 to og-knob-4 and its button is og-aux \, so the two surfaces can never be confused for one another. One line here if it reads badly on the screen., f 58;
#X text 1200 1950 ⛔ THE AUX BUTTON IS A MODIFIER \, NOT A CONTROL. It publishes no name on param at all \, so nothing in the map can bind it and it cannot report itself raw on disp the way an unmapped control would. What it does is hold \$0-shift \, which moves the keyboard onto its second layer -- og-shift-60 to og-shift-84 instead of og-key-60 to og-key-84. ⚠️ BOTH EDGES ARE USED NOW \, where select 1 used to take the press and drop the release on purpose: a modifier that cannot be let go of is not a modifier. It was the transport until start and stop went back to the nano's PLAY and STOP \, which is what freed the only button on this panel that can never be the missing device., f 58;
#X text 20 950 A MESSAGE BOX NEEDS NO list trim. og-knob-1 \$1 already has og-knob-1 as its SELECTOR \, which is the shape route matches -- so the list prepend / list trim chain that m_nano needs is simply absent here. In a message box \$1 is the incoming value \; in an object box it would be a creation argument., f 58;
#X text 640 520 THE PRESENCE OUTLET IS RIGHTMOST ON EVERY TRIGGER HERE \, so it fires FIRST: seen \, then the value. That order is not arbitrary -- mother having spoken at all is true whatever the value turns out to mean \, so it is the one claim that cannot be made wrong by anything below it. Action before report otherwise \, the same way u_init sequences its stages. ⚠️ THERE ARE THREE SOURCES AND EACH HAS ITS OWN: the aux button beside this comment \, the four knobs \, and the keyboard., f 44;
#X text 640 780 EVERY KNOB GOES THROUGH change -1. ✅ MOTHER PUSHES ONCE AT LOAD AND THEN SAYS NOTHING -- measured on the device 2026-08-08 \, one KNOB1 print in twelve seconds with nobody touching it. Item 237 \, and parameter pickup in u_map depends on it: if mother streamed \, the first value would be spent on its own reading and pickup would never arm. THE -1 IS LOAD-BEARING: a bare change starts life holding 0 \, so a knob physically parked at 0 would never publish at all and the tempo would sit at its default. -1 cannot be a real value here \, since mother's knobs are 0 to 1. Measured \, not reasoned -- the bare form swallowed the first value in testing, f 60;
#X text 640 1060 WHAT IS NOT HERE: the encoder \, encbut \, the keyboard and the pedal jack. The encoder is contested with mother's own menu through enableSubMenu \, and none of the others has anything to drive yet. They belong in THIS file when they do -- it is one device \, so it is one m_ abstraction., f 44;
#X text 20 1250 ⛔ THE KNOBS NO LONGER REPORT TO disp \, and og-aux still does. A knob's RAW 0-to-1 position is not a readable parameter row -- the screen said og-knob-1 0.245 where a BPM belonged \, and the param layer replaces the footer \, so the tempo it was mapped to vanished while you turned it. u_map reports the value instead \, because it is the only file that knows what a control MEANS: the mapped value when there is a mapping and the raw one when there is not. ⚠️ AN UNMAPPED KNOB STILL REPORTS \, and an earlier version of this comment claimed the opposite. A control that does nothing and says nothing cannot be told from a broken one. Item 242. ⚠️ og-aux keeps its own report because the transport is not a mapped value, f 62;
#X msg 440 560 seen m_organelle;
#X obj 440 620 s presence;
#X obj 1000 1200 loadbang;
#X msg 1000 1260 expect m_organelle passive;
#X obj 1000 1320 s presence;
#X text 1100 950 LIVENESS OFF THE FAN-IN \, WHICH IS THE ONLY PLACE IT COULD GO. There is no channel gate here and no reply to match -- mother publishes on reserved global names and this file simply receives them \, so the arrival of ANY of the five IS the evidence. ⚠️ It is weaker evidence than the other two devices give \, and the kind field says so., f 40;
#X text 1000 1400 ⛔ PASSIVE IS A KIND ON THE PRESENCE BUS \, NOT A SILENCE. m_organelle registers itself and publishes seen \, and it instantiates NO c_presence -- so nothing ages it and it can never be declared lost. ✅ MOTHER PUSHES THE KNOBS ONCE AT LOAD AND THEN SAYS NOTHING -- item 237 \, measured -- so a last-heard clock here would run out a few seconds into EVERY boot and put a device-lost warning on the screen for hardware that is bolted to the instrument. ⛔ AND THAT IS EXACTLY WHY THE KNOBS MUST PUBLISH seen: they are the ONLY thing mother ever sends unprompted \, so a knob path that skipped it left this layer reading never-seen forever on a device where it had in fact spoken. It did \, from item 242 until g_oled's diag layer read the bus and showed it. What a passive layer can offer is LAST HEARD \; what it cannot offer is the difference between unplugged and untouched \, and no amount of code here changes that -- the operator supplies it. See ref/module/presence.md., f 44;
#X obj 1330 300 r notes;
#X obj 1330 360 unpack f f;
#X obj 2400 900 makefilename og-key-%d;
#X obj 1600 520 pack s f;
#X obj 1600 590 t a a;
#X obj 1600 650 list trim;
#X obj 1600 710 s param;
#X text 1600 780 THE KEYBOARD \, AND THE COMMENT BELOW USED TO SAY IT WAS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. It was \, because none of the omitted controls had anything to drive yet -- and that is the whole condition it named: "They belong in THIS file when they do." This is the when. ⛔ notes IS ONE OF MOTHER'S OWN NAMES \, not a C-2 allowlist name \, and reading it here is legitimate for exactly the reason led and oscOut are: mother publishes on reserved global names and the m_ layer that owns the device is the file allowed to read them. Do not "fix" it into the allowlist., f 62;
#X text 1600 1000 ONE CONTROL PER KEY \, WHICH IS WHAT THE ONE-VALUE RULE WANTS. mother packs the keyboard into ONE two-float list -- pitch then velocity -- and param carries exactly one value per control. So the PITCH rides in the control NAME and the velocity is the value: og-key-60 through og-key-84 \, since the Organelle's lowest key is note 60 and it has 25 of them. That is also what makes "these eight keys play the Volca and those two fire 404 pads" expressible at all. ⚠️ A RELEASE IS VELOCITY 0 AND IS PUBLISHED \, unlike aux \, which is press-only: a note-off is a real event that a destination has to act on \, where a button release means nothing., f 62;
#X text 1600 1300 unpack FIRES RIGHT TO LEFT \, so the velocity is parked in pack's cold inlet before the pitch arrives to build the name and trigger it. Same guarantee u_map's arg-then-value ordering rests on. ⛔ THE list trim IS LOAD-BEARING: pack emits a LIST \, whose selector is list rather than the control name \, and u_map's route matches a SELECTOR (C-6). Without it every key takes the reject and is divided by 127 into nothing -- silent in both directions., f 62;
#X text 1600 1560 ⛔ THE KEYS DO NOT REACH disp \, and that is the same decision the knobs made for a sharper reason. g_oled holds five parameter rows \, so a two-handed chord would evict everything else on the screen twice per note -- once on the press and once on the release. ⚠️ AND u_map DOES NOT REPORT THEM RAW EITHER \, which is a deliberate exception to item 242: see ref/module/map.md., f 62;
#X msg 1980 240 seen m_organelle;
#X obj 1980 300 s presence;
#X connect 3 0 8 0;
#X connect 4 0 9 0;
#X connect 5 0 10 0;
#X connect 6 0 11 0;
#X connect 7 0 12 0;
#X connect 8 0 13 0;
#X connect 9 0 14 0;
#X connect 10 0 15 0;
#X connect 11 0 16 0;
#X connect 27 0 28 0;
#X connect 29 0 30 0;
#X connect 30 0 31 0;
#X connect 34 0 35 0;
#X connect 36 0 37 0;
#X connect 37 0 38 0;
#X connect 38 1 45 0;
#X connect 45 0 46 0;
#X connect 38 0 39 0;
#X connect 39 0 40 0;
#X obj 260 470 t a b;
#X text 260 1560 ⛔ THE KNOBS' OWN FAN-IN \, AND IT IS A REGRESSION FIX. Every source used to converge on the t a b b below \, which is what published seen \; item 242 took the knobs off disp and rewired them straight to param \, and the presence publish went with them silently. og-aux and the keys still had theirs \, so m_organelle only looked alive if you pressed something -- and mother's boot push of the four knobs \, the one thing it sends without being asked \, said nothing at all. Nothing could see it until there was a screen that drew last-heard. b before a \, so seen goes out before the value., f 44;
#X connect 47 0 19 0;
#X connect 47 1 27 0;
#X connect 13 0 47 0;
#X connect 14 0 47 0;
#X connect 15 0 47 0;
#X connect 16 0 47 0;
#X obj 20 360 t f f f;
#X obj 20 440 s \$0-shift;
#X msg 560 480 modal-off;
#X obj 1330 580 != 0;
#X obj 1330 640 s \$0-press;
#X obj 2400 300 t f f;
#X obj 2560 360 s \$0-pitch;
#X obj 2400 420 - 60;
#X obj 2400 480 t f f f;
#X obj 2120 600 tabwrite \$0-shifted;
#X obj 2700 540 t b;
#X obj 2700 600 f;
#X obj 2860 560 r \$0-shift;
#X obj 2700 660 spigot;
#X obj 2860 620 r \$0-press;
#X obj 2400 720 tabread \$0-shifted;
#X obj 2400 780 select 0 1;
#X obj 2400 840 f;
#X obj 2560 800 r \$0-pitch;
#X obj 2900 840 f;
#X obj 3060 800 r \$0-pitch;
#X obj 2900 900 makefilename og-shift-%d;
#X obj 3500 300 array define \$0-shifted 25;
#X text 20 1950 ⛔ A RELEASE MUST CARRY THE NAME ITS PRESS DID \, and nothing else in this file is as easy to get wrong. Press a shifted key \, let go of aux \, then let go of the key: the press published og-shift-72 and the release would publish og-key-72. The shifted control never sees its note-off \, and an unshifted one gets a note-off it never had a note-on for -- in mode 1 that is A STUCK NOTE ON THE VOLCA \, and nothing anywhere reports it. So the layer is latched PER KEY \, AT PRESS TIME: a 25-element array indexed by pitch minus 60 \, written only when the velocity is non-zero \, and read on BOTH edges. A release then cannot disagree with its own press however the modifier moves underneath it. Same shape as u_map's pickup arrays \, and for the same reason., f 84;
#X text 2400 1020 THE ORDER IS VALUE \, PITCH \, INDEX \, WRITE \, READ \, and every step of it is a trigger firing right to left. unpack gives the velocity first \, so \$0-press is decided before the pitch arrives \; the pitch is stored before it becomes an index \; the index reaches tabwrite's COLD inlet before the write fires \; and the read runs last \, on the value the write may just have put there. C-3: a fan-out gets a trigger even where the order happens to work., f 62;
#X text 3500 380 25 ELEMENTS \, ONE PER KEY \, and the index is pitch minus 60 because the lowest key is note 60 -- item 293. An array rather than one flag is what makes a CHORD safe: two keys held across a change of modifier keep their own layers independently of each other., f 58;
